---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const emailModular = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=Modular%20creative%20production%20%E2%80%94%20tell%20us%20about%20your%20brand";
const emailGeneral = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=Modular%20creative%20inquiry";
const calHref = "https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first";
---

<Layout
  title="Modular Creative — The Complete Guide to Component-Based Ad Production | OKAD"
  description="Modular creative is producing ad components (hooks, bodies, CTAs) separately and combining them into dozens of unique variations. This guide covers the math, production workflow, testing approach, naming conventions, and how to scale winners."
>
  <Header />
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-20 md:pt-24 pb-10 text-center bg-bg">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[12px] font-medium text-accent bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.18)] rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 mb-6">
          Open reference &middot; September 2026
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(28px,5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink mb-4">
          Modular Creative: <span class="text-accent">The Complete Guide</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-[18px] text-ink-2 max-w-[600px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-8">
          Modular creative is producing ad components &mdash; hooks, bodies, CTAs &mdash; separately and combining them into dozens of unique variations. 6 hooks &times; 4 bodies &times; 3 CTAs = 72 unique ads from just 13 components. This guide covers how to build and scale a modular production system.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap mb-8">
          <a href={emailModular} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-hover transition-all no-underline">Order modular creative &rarr;</a>
          <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-card text-ink border border-border hover:border-accent hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5 flex-wrap justify-center font-mono text-[12px] text-muted">
          <span>13 components &rarr; 72 ads</span>
          <span>80%+ cost reduction</span>
          <span>Hook-first testing</span>
          <span>Component analytics</span>
          <span>Systematic naming</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works grid -->
    <section class="py-8">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-center mb-5">How Modular Creative Works</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5">
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F9E9;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Shoot Components, Not Ads</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Produce hooks, bodies, and CTAs as separate pieces. Combine them in the edit into dozens of unique variations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F4CA;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Test at the Component Level</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Discover which specific hook, body, or CTA drives performance. Not which "ad" wins &mdash; which component wins.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F680;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Scale Winning Components</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Found a winning hook? Attach it to every body. Found a winning body? Test it with new hooks. Compound learnings.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <section class="py-10 border-t border-b border-border">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-muted-2 mb-4">Contents</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-1.5">
          {[
            { num: "01", text: "Overview", href: "#overview" },
            { num: "02", text: "What Is Modular Creative?", href: "#what" },
            { num: "03", text: "The Math", href: "#math" },
            { num: "04", text: "Components", href: "#components" },
            { num: "05", text: "Production Workflow", href: "#workflow" },
            { num: "06", text: "Testing Approach", href: "#testing" },
            { num: "07", text: "Modular vs Traditional Production", href: "#comparison" },
            { num: "08", text: "Naming, Storage & Analytics", href: "#naming" },
            { num: "09", text: "Scaling Winners", href: "#scaling" },
            { num: "10", text: "Glossary", href: "#glossary" },
            { num: "11", text: "FAQ", href: "#faq" },
          ].map((item) => (
            <a href={item.href} class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[14px] text-ink-2 font-medium hover:bg-bg-alt transition-colors no-underline">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium text-accent min-w-[22px]">{item.num}</span>
              {item.text}
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 01 Overview -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="overview">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">01 &mdash; Overview</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Stop producing ads. Start producing components.</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Modular creative = producing hooks, bodies, CTAs as separate components</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">13 components can generate 72 unique ad variations</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Cuts production cost 80%+ vs shooting individual ads</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Traditional ad production creates finished, monolithic ads. If the hook doesn't work, the entire ad is wasted. If the body is strong but the CTA is weak, you can't fix it without re-shooting. Every ad is a single bet &mdash; and most bets lose.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Modular creative flips this model. Instead of shooting finished ads, you produce individual components: hooks (the first 3 seconds), body narratives (the middle), and CTAs (the closing). Then you combine them in the edit to create dozens of unique variations. If a hook fails, you swap it &mdash; without re-shooting the body or CTA.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This approach is the production backbone of <a href="/performance-creative" class="text-accent hover:underline">performance creative</a>. It's how brands producing 20&ndash;50+ new ads per month do it at a fraction of the cost of traditional production.</p>
        <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">What:</strong> component-based ad production (hooks, bodies, CTAs)</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Why:</strong> 72 ad variations from 13 components; 80%+ cost reduction</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">How:</strong> shoot components separately, combine in the edit</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Key benefit:</strong> test and iterate at the component level, not the ad level</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 What Is Modular Creative -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="what">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">02 &mdash; Definition</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What is modular creative?</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">A production system where ads are built from interchangeable parts</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Each part (hook, body, CTA) is designed to work with any other</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Component-level data tells you which piece drives performance</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Modular creative</strong> is a production methodology where video ads are assembled from interchangeable components rather than produced as single, complete units. Each component &mdash; hook, body narrative, product demo, social proof clip, CTA &mdash; is designed to connect with any other component in the system.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">A quick example</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A supplement brand shoots a production session with three creators. Each creator records: 4 different hook openings, 2 body narratives (one about energy, one about sleep), 2 product demo clips, and 2 CTAs. That's 10 components per creator, 30 total. The editor combines these into 4 &times; 2 &times; 2 &times; 2 = 32 unique ad variations per creator, 96 total. The test spend to run all 96 variations: $4,800 at $50/day each for 1 day. Within a week, the team knows exactly which hooks, which body narratives, and which CTAs drive the lowest CPA.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">What modular creative is not</h3>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Not random variation</strong> &mdash; each component is designed to connect with others. Random edits create Frankenstein ads.</li>
          <li><strong>Not dynamic creative optimization (DCO)</strong> &mdash; DCO is platform-side automated variation. Modular creative is production-side intentional variation.</li>
          <li><strong>Not just different thumbnails</strong> &mdash; true modular production changes the video content, not just the visual packaging.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 The Math -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="math">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">03 &mdash; The Math</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">The math: exponential output from linear production</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">6 hooks &times; 4 bodies &times; 3 CTAs = 72 unique combinations</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Traditional cost for 72 ads: $36K+. Modular cost: $5K&ndash;$8K.</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Every new component multiplies the total output</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6 my-6 text-center">
          <div class="font-mono text-[18px] font-bold text-accent mb-2">6 Hooks &times; 4 Bodies &times; 3 CTAs = 72 Unique Ads</div>
          <p class="text-[14px] text-muted m-0">From just 13 individual components</p>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Cost comparison</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Approach</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Components / Ads</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Unique Variations</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Est. Production Cost</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Traditional (individual ads)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">72 finished ads</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">72</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">$36,000+ ($500/ad)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Modular (component-based)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">13 components</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">72</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">$5,000&ndash;$8,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Savings</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">&mdash;</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Same output</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2 font-semibold" style="color: #2e7d32">80%+ reduction</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The compounding effect</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The math gets more powerful over time. If you add 3 new hooks next week, you don't add 3 ads &mdash; you add 3 &times; 4 &times; 3 = 36 new unique combinations. Every new component multiplies the total output. This is why modular production scales better than traditional production over time.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 Components -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="components">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">04 &mdash; Components</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">The six component types</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Hooks: the first 3 seconds &mdash; highest leverage, test first</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Bodies: the core narrative (5&ndash;20 seconds)</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">CTAs, product demos, social proof clips, and supers/text overlays</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Component</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Duration</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Purpose</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Testing Priority</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Hooks</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">0&ndash;3 seconds</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Stop the scroll. Create curiosity or recognition.</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2 font-semibold" style="color: #c62828">Highest</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Body narratives</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">5&ndash;20 seconds</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Deliver the core message: problem, solution, benefit.</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2 font-semibold" style="color: #f57f17">High</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Product demos</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">5&ndash;15 seconds</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Show the product working. Screen recordings, unboxings.</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2 font-semibold" style="color: #f57f17">High</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Social proof clips</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">3&ndash;8 seconds</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Testimonials, review quotes, usage stats.</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Medium</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">CTAs</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">2&ndash;5 seconds</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Close the ad: "Try it free," "Link in bio," "Get 20% off."</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Lower</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Supers / text overlays</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Throughout</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Reinforce key messages. Essential for sound-off viewing.</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Variable</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Design for interchangeability</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The key to modular creative is designing components that connect cleanly. Hooks should end with a natural transition point. Bodies should start without referencing specific hooks. CTAs should work regardless of which body precedes them. This requires scripting discipline &mdash; each component is self-contained but designed to flow into any adjacent piece.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 Production Workflow -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="workflow">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">05 &mdash; Workflow</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Production workflow</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Shoot all hooks in one session, all demos in another</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Script for modularity &mdash; each piece must work independently</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Edit combinations systematically using the naming convention</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The five production stages</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Script modular concepts.</strong> Write scripts where each section (hook, body, CTA) is a standalone module. Include transition notes so editors know where components connect. Mark which components are interchangeable.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Batch-shoot hooks.</strong> All hooks for one concept in a single session. Same creator, same setup, different openings. Shoot 6&ndash;10 hook variants &mdash; hooks are the highest-leverage component. For <a href="/hook-rate" class="text-accent hover:underline">hook rate</a> optimization, shoot multiple hook types: questions, stats, before/after, controversy.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Batch-shoot bodies and demos.</strong> Separate sessions for body narratives, product demonstrations, testimonials, and CTAs. Each body should start with a clean transition that works after any hook.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Assemble combinations.</strong> Edit hook + body + CTA combinations using a systematic approach. Use the naming convention (Section 08) to track every variation. An editor can produce 20&ndash;40 combinations per day with properly organized components.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>QC and export.</strong> Review each combination for flow and timing. Export in platform-specific formats: 9:16 for Reels/TikTok/Shorts, 1:1 for feed, 16:9 for YouTube in-stream. Apply text overlays appropriate to each platform.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Mid CTA -->
    <section class="py-10">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bg-dark rounded-2xl p-10 md:p-14 text-center">
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(22px,3.5vw,32px)] tracking-[-0.02em] text-white mb-3">Want OKAD to build your modular creative library?</h2>
          <p class="text-[15px] text-muted max-w-[480px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-6">We produce component libraries for brands: hooks, bodies, demos, CTAs. You get dozens of tested ad variations from a single production session &mdash; with data on which components drive performance.</p>
          <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap">
            <a href={emailModular} class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-white text-ink hover:bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Order modular creative &rarr;</a>
            <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold text-muted border border-white/15 hover:text-white hover:border-white/30 transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 06 Testing Approach -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="testing">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">06 &mdash; Testing</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Testing approach: hooks first, then bodies, then CTAs</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Test hooks first &mdash; they have the highest leverage on performance</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Keep everything else constant when testing one component type</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Component-level testing produces 3x the learnings of ad-level testing</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Modular creative enables a fundamentally different testing approach. Instead of testing "which ad wins," you test "which component wins." This produces far more actionable data because you can isolate exactly which element drives performance.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The testing sequence</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Test hooks.</strong> Keep the same body and CTA. Run 6 hook variants. Measure <a href="/hook-rate" class="text-accent hover:underline">hook rate</a> and early CPA. Identify the top 2&ndash;3 hooks.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Test bodies.</strong> Attach the winning hooks to 4 different body narratives. Keep the CTA constant. Measure CPA and conversion rate. Identify the top 1&ndash;2 bodies.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Test CTAs.</strong> Attach winning hook + winning body to 3 different CTAs. Measure CPA. CTAs have the smallest marginal impact, so test them last.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Scale the winning combination.</strong> The best hook + best body + best CTA is your champion ad. Produce variations of this combination: new creators, different angles on the same hook, minor edits.</li>
        </ol>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4 mt-6">This follows the same <a href="/guide" class="text-accent hover:underline">creative testing</a> hierarchy: test the highest-leverage variable first, find the winner, then move to the next level. Each stage builds on the previous winner, compounding learnings.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 07 Modular vs Traditional -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="comparison">
