    <!-- 08 Naming, Storage & Analytics -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="naming">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">08 &mdash; Naming &amp; Analytics</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Naming conventions, storage, and component analytics</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Naming: [concept]_[hook-variant]_[body-variant]_[cta-variant]</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Consistent naming enables component-level analytics</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Tag components to identify which piece drives performance</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The naming convention</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A consistent naming convention is non-negotiable for modular creative at scale. Without it, you can't tell which components are in which ad, and you lose the ability to analyze at the component level.</p>

        <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6 my-6">
          <div class="font-mono text-[14px] font-semibold text-accent mb-2">Format: [concept]_[hook]_[body]_[cta]</div>
          <div class="space-y-1 text-[13px] text-muted">
            <p class="m-0"><strong class="text-ink">Example:</strong> skincare-routine_hook-question_body-beforeafter_cta-tryfree</p>
            <p class="m-0"><strong class="text-ink">Example:</strong> productivity-app_hook-stat_body-demo_cta-linkinbio</p>
            <p class="m-0"><strong class="text-ink">Example:</strong> energy-supplement_hook-controversy_body-testimonial_cta-20off</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Component-level analytics</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">With consistent naming, you can aggregate performance data by component. Instead of asking "which ad won?" you can ask more powerful questions:</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Which hook performs best across all body combinations?</strong> &mdash; aggregating CPA for all ads with "hook-question" shows hook-level performance</li>
          <li><strong>Which body converts best regardless of hook?</strong> &mdash; aggregating CPA for all ads with "body-demo" reveals body-level performance</li>
          <li><strong>What is the single best combination?</strong> &mdash; the winning hook + winning body + winning CTA, identified through component-level data</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Storage and organization</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Organize your asset library by component type, not by ad. Folders: Hooks, Bodies, Demos, Social Proof, CTAs, Supers. Within each folder, use the naming convention. Tag components with metadata: concept, creator, date, platform, hook type. This makes it fast to find and reuse winning components in future combinations.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 09 Scaling Winners -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="scaling">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; Scaling</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Scaling winners: more variations of what works</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Found a winning hook? Create 5 more variations in that style</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Winning components get more variations; losing components get replaced</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Modular scaling extends creative life and delays <a href="/ad-fatigue" class="text-accent hover:underline">ad fatigue</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Once you've identified winning components, the scaling strategy is straightforward: produce more variations of what works and attach them to other winning components. This extends the creative's lifespan and multiplies the output of your testing program.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Scaling playbook</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Winning hook &rarr; more hook variations.</strong> If "stat hooks" win, produce 5 more stat hooks with different numbers, different framings, different creators. Test each with the winning body.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Winning body &rarr; attach to new hooks.</strong> If a product demo body outperforms, attach it to every hook type you haven't tested yet. This may unlock combinations you hadn't considered.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>New creators on winning scripts.</strong> Have different creators perform the same winning hook + body combination. Creator variation extends the creative's life with each new audience.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Minor edits on fatiguing winners.</strong> When a winning ad starts to fatigue, produce small variations: new text overlays, different music, slightly re-cut timing. These minor edits can extend lifespan by 1&ndash;2 weeks before a full refresh is needed.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6 my-6 flex gap-4 items-start flex-col sm:flex-row">
          <div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-[10px] bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.12)] flex items-center justify-center text-[20px] shrink-0">&#9889;</div>
